<title>USA: Computer Horizons names successor for CFO.</title>
<headline>Computer Horizons names successor for CFO.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNTAIN LAKES, N.J. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Horizons Corp said Thursday that William Murphy will become chief financial officer effective January 2.</p>
<p>Murphy succeeds Bernhard Hubert, who is retiring but will continue in a consulting role, the company said.</p>
<p>Commputer Horizons said Murphy is a partner of Grant Thornton LLP, its auditors.</p>
